{{- /* mcp_mounts renders an agent's/task's MCP tool sources (N40): one
MCPToolset per source, on the tools surface. An absent field emits no argument,
so the SDK's own default stands: no transport_type means it reads the URL (a
path ending in /mcp is streamable HTTP), no allowed_tools means every tool the
server exposes, no headers means no authentication.

The two timeouts are the exception, and they are written out because leaving
them off makes the same package behave differently on the two targets.
MCPServerHTTP defaults both to 5 seconds, which no web search or crawl answers
inside; Pipecat's MCP client defaults to 30. 30 wins because it is the value one
target already had, so this closes the gap without inventing a number. A tool
slower than that needs `timeout:` on the mcp block, which does not exist yet. */ -}}
